  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "The mirror – slide steps against an attacker",
  "description": "Set up two corridors on the half court, each about four metres wide with a cone at each end. Players work in pairs: the attacker stands with their back to the half-court line and the defender an arm's length in front, between the attacker and the basket. The attacker moves sideways between the cones, changes speed and direction and fakes with shoulders and hips. The defender mirrors every move in a defensive stance with slide steps, without crossing the feet and without standing up. Go for 15–20 seconds, switch roles, and bring in the next pair.\n\nProgression: first without the ball, then the attacker dribbles sideways. Final step: when the coach claps, it becomes a live 1 v 1 to the basket, one pair at a time. Variation: the attacker starts without the ball by the cone, the coach passes and the defender closes out from the basket before the mirroring starts. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Low and wide – never cross your feet; slide with short steps and lead with the foot on the side you are going."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Watch the attacker's hips and belly button, not the ball or the head."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Keep your head at the same height all the time – bouncing up and down makes you late."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Attacker: vary the speed and try stopping dead – you are the one making the mirror better."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
